1. Frontend Deployment to AWS S3 + CloudFront
Purpose

This workflow:

Builds the frontend application
Uploads build artifacts to S3
Invalidates CloudFront cache
Sends deployment status notifications
AWS Resources Required

Create the following AWS resources:

Amazon S3 Bucket

Used to host frontend static files.

Amazon CloudFront Distribution

Used as a CDN to serve content globally.

Architecture
GitHub Actions
        │
        ▼
    Amazon S3
        │
        ▼
   CloudFront CDN
        │
        ▼
       Users
IAM User Requirements

Create a dedicated IAM user for deployments.

Generate:

Access Key ID
Secret Access Key
Required IAM Permissions

Example deployment policy:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:*"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "cloudfront:CreateInvalidation",
        "cloudfront:GetDistribution"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}

For production environments, permissions should be restricted to specific resources.

Frontend Project Requirements

The project should contain:

{
  "scripts": {
    "build": "...",
    "test": "..."
  }
}

Expected build output:

dist/

The deployment workflow uploads:

aws s3 sync ./dist s3://bucket-name --delete
Required GitHub Secrets
Secret Name	Description
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID	AWS IAM Access Key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY	AWS IAM Secret Key
AWS_REGION	AWS Region
S3_BUCKET	S3 Bucket Name
CLOUDFRONT_ID	CloudFront Distribution ID
SMTP_USERNAME	Email Sender Address
SMTP_PASSWORD	SMTP Password / App Password
EMAIL_TO	Recipient Email Address(es)
Example
AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
S3_BUCKET=my-frontend-bucket
CLOUDFRONT_ID=E123ABC456XYZ


2. Email Notification Configuration
Purpose

Email notifications are sent when a deployment:

Succeeds
Fails
Gets cancelled

Notifications include:

Repository information
Branch information
Deployment result
Commit details
Workflow execution link

GitHub Secrets

Store:

SMTP_USERNAME=your-email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=<generated-app-password>
EMAIL_TO=team@company.com

Note: Do not use your normal Gmail password.